## FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES (Top Mistakes — ⚠️ DEFAULT inferred from goal)

### Pattern 1: Sync vs Async for High-Volume Use Cases

❌ **BAD** (Top Mistake #1 — sync REST for 50K+/day):
> "We'll use a synchronous REST callout from Apex on Claim insert to push the claim to Guidewire ClaimsCenter."

**Why wrong**: 50K claims/day = ~2.9 TPS sustained, ~14.5 TPS peak. Sync REST in Apex blocks the transaction, hits 10s callout limit, fails on Guidewire downtime, blocks user UI. Will fail under burst.

✅ **GOOD**:
> "Publish a `Claim_Created__e` Platform Event on Claim insert; a MuleSoft subscriber consumes the event, transforms to Guidewire ClaimSpec, and POSTs to ClaimsCenter with retry + dead-letter via SQS. Trade-off table below shows why Platform Event over CDC: Platform Event allows enriched payload at publish time; CDC fires on every record mutation (noisier)."

**Why right**: Async decouples SFDC transaction from Guidewire availability; replay covers 72h outage; trade-off table cites the alternative considered.

### Pattern 2: Industry Cloud Objects vs Stock Objects

❌ **BAD** (Top Mistake #2 — using Case for claims):
> "Claims will be modeled as Case records with custom fields for ClaimNumber__c, PolicyHolder__c, etc."

**Why wrong**: Case is generic. FSC Insurance has `Claim`, `ClaimParticipant`, `ClaimCoverage`, `InsurancePolicy` objects with built-in relationships, regulatory reporting templates, and Industry Cloud roadmap alignment. Custom-fielding Case re-invents the wheel and breaks at scale.

✅ **GOOD**:
> "Use FSC Insurance objects: `Claim` (header), `ClaimParticipant` (claimants/beneficiaries), `ClaimCoverage` (coverage applied), linked to `InsurancePolicy`. Custom object only for Guidewire-specific extensions (e.g., `Guidewire_Reserve__c`) where no FSC field exists. Trade-off table compares FSC vs custom in Section 4."

**Why right**: Leverages out-of-box FSC features; aligns with vendor roadmap; custom objects only where genuinely needed.

### Pattern 3: PII/PHI Encryption in Regulated Industries

❌ **BAD** (Top Mistake #3 — skipping encryption mention):
> "Standard SFDC field-level security and profile permissions will protect claimant data."

**Why wrong**: HIPAA/PHI requires field-level encryption at rest (Shield Platform Encryption), not just access control. Profile permissions don't encrypt — they only restrict UI/API visibility. Auditors will flag.

✅ **GOOD**:
> "Apply Shield Platform Encryption to PHI fields: `Claim.Diagnosis__c`, `ClaimParticipant.SSN__c`, `ClaimParticipant.DateOfBirth__c`. Field Audit Trail enabled on all PHI fields (HIPAA §164.312(b)). Sharing model: OWD = Private on `Claim`; sharing rules grant claim handlers access via role hierarchy. SOC 2 + HIPAA BAA in place with Salesforce. See compliance posture table in Section 8."

**Why right**: Names specific Shield encryption + Field Audit Trail + sharing model + cites HIPAA paragraph + references compliance posture.

