## MERMAID DIAGRAM STANDARDS (mandatory for Section 3)

> **Canonical source**: `r-genie/Agent_Builder/lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md`. The 10 non-negotiable rules below are the agent-facing summary; full rationale + edge cases in the canonical doc.

### The 10 Rules

1. **`<br/>` for line breaks in node/edge labels** — NEVER `\n` (renders literal `\n` in GitHub/Cursor/Windsurf)
2. **Init directive REQUIRED** for `flowchart` and `graph` — start every block with:
   ```
   %%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%
   ```
   Default curved bezier edges overlap in dense diagrams. Linear is the only safe default.
3. **stateDiagram-v2 does NOT need init directive** — different rendering pipeline
4. **Declare nodes upstream → downstream** (left-to-right or top-to-bottom in execution order)
5. **Group connections logically** — primary path first, then branches; blank line between groups
6. **Arrow semantics consistent**: solid `-->` for forward progression; dashed `-.->` for back-edges/retries/async returns only
7. **Edge labels short** — action / protocol / event names; no full sentences; no redundant labels on fan-out
8. **All `style` declarations at the END** of the diagram, in node-declaration order — never interleaved
9. **No dangling nodes** — every declared node must have at least one connection
10. **Pre-emit self-check (12 items)** runs in `@03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` SELF-CHECK before any Mermaid block ships

### Section 3 (Architecture Diagram) Specifics

For the Salesforce Architecture Diagram:
- **Diagram type**: `flowchart TB` (top-bottom for system layers) OR `graph LR` (left-right for data flow)
- **Suggested layers**: External Systems (top) → Integration Layer (middle) → SFDC Clouds (bottom)
- **Show explicitly**: integration platform (MuleSoft/Boomi/etc.) as named middle node; named SFDC clouds (FSC, Service Cloud); external partners (Guidewire, SAP); event bus / queue components
- **Style classes**: differentiate SFDC (blue), middleware (orange), external (gray) — declared at end

### Skeleton

```
%%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%
flowchart TB
    GW[Guidewire<br/>ClaimsCenter]
    MS[MuleSoft<br/>Anypoint]
    SQS[AWS SQS<br/>Dead-Letter]
    PE[(Platform Event<br/>Claim_Created__e)]
    FSC[FSC Insurance<br/>Claim Object]
    SC[Service Cloud<br/>Case Routing]

    FSC --> PE
    PE --> MS
    MS -->|POST ClaimSpec| GW
    MS -.->|on failure| SQS
    GW -->|status update| MS
    MS --> SC

    style FSC fill:#1798c1,color:#fff
    style SC fill:#1798c1,color:#fff
    style MS fill:#ff6b35,color:#fff
    style GW fill:#666,color:#fff
    style SQS fill:#666,color:#fff
    style PE fill:#9c27b0,color:#fff
```

