## PROGRESSIVE DOCUMENTATION v2 — FIVE MECHANICS (mandatory)

> **Source of truth**: `r-genie/Agent_Builder/lib/docs/prompt-engineering-patterns.md` Pattern #20 v2. Adapted below for this agent's domain.

### Mechanic 1 — Template-First Skeleton (Phase 0)
Phase 0 creates the deliverable file with all 12 section headings + `<!-- SECTION: kebab-case -->` markers + `_{pending Phase N}_` placeholders. Zero analytical content. Markers double as `old_string` anchors for later targeted `edit` operations.

### Mechanic 2 — Per-Phase Write Contract
Every generation phase (1-7) writes its approved section(s) to the corresponding marker(s) BEFORE its checkpoint. The Phase Orchestration Per-Phase Write Contract table is the single source of truth. See `@01_Phase_Orchestration.mdc`.

### Mechanic 3 — Preview-in-Chat → Approve → Write-Clean-to-File
For each generation phase:
1. **Preview substance** in chat (compact bullets/table — never full prose)
2. **STOP and WAIT** for user approval/correction
3. **After approval**, write clean prose to section marker via `edit` (pre-read first)
4. **3-5 line confirmation** in chat (section name, line count, file path) — never re-dump prose

### Mechanic 4 — Phase 8 = Consolidate & Polish (NOT From-Scratch)
Phase 8 mode is **CONSOLIDATE**:
- Re-read persisted file
- Cross-section consistency edits (entity names, vendor naming, terminology)
- Replace residual `_{pending Phase N}_` placeholders
- Verify zero standalone `<!-- SECTION: ... -->` markers remain
- Final style/length self-check against verbosity anchor

**Forbidden in Phase 8**: regenerating sections already written and approved in Phases 0-7.

### Mechanic 5 — What Stays in Chat vs File
- **To file**: approved section prose, Mermaid block, Lucidchart instructions, risk register, references
- **In chat**: previews (compact), approval prompts, validation report, polish summary, dual-author footer is in file only

### Per-Edit Size Budget

| Budget | When |
|--------|------|
| **≤300 lines per `edit`** | Standard target |
| **≤500 lines** | Absolute ceiling — only structurally indivisible sections |
| **Split further** | If content >300 lines, multiple `edit` calls within the same phase |

