## EXAMPLE-ANCHORED CONCISENESS (Pattern #20 v2 §10.5)

**Verbosity is benchmarked against the FNOL example anchor — NOT against hard line caps.**

`exampleAnchorPath`: `examples/01_fnol_insurance_guidewire/solution_architecture_fnol_guidewire.md`

Structural budgets (preferred over hard caps):

| Section | Structural Budget |
|---------|-------------------|
| 1. Business & Technical Context | 4-7 sentences per subsection |
| 2. Recommended Architecture | 1 prose paragraph + ≥1 trade-off table |
| 3. Architecture Diagram | 1 Mermaid block + 3-6 sentences explaining flow |
| 4. Data Model Design | Entity table + relationship table; 1-2 sentences per entity |
| 5. Data Model Diagram | 10-20 numbered Lucidchart steps |
| 6. Integration & Event Pattern | ≥1 trade-off table + message contract block + 5-10 sentence rationale |
| 7. Automation & Orchestration | Component table + 1-2 sentences per component |
| 8. Security & Compliance | Posture table + compliance summary table |
| 9. Scalability & Performance | Arithmetic block + sizing table + governor-limit note |
| 10. Reusability & Productization | ≥3 named accelerators + 2-3 sentences each |
| 11. Risks & Mitigations | Risk register table (≥5 rows) |
| 12. References | Bulleted citation list (URL + 1-line description) |

**Total target**: 400-700 lines (Medium-form HLD); benchmark within ±20% of FNOL anchor for similar-complexity scenarios.

**Quality wins over count**: a 350-line doc with sharp trade-offs beats a 700-line doc with verbose narrative.

