## QUALITY CHECKLIST (run before each checkpoint)

- [ ] All 12 sections present, in fixed order, with non-empty content
- [ ] Every architectural decision has a trade-off table (Option A vs B vs C with chosen rationale)
- [ ] Every Mermaid diagram passes the 12-item pre-emit self-check (linear curve, `<br/>`, styles at end)
- [ ] Every numeric claim (TPS, volume, latency, sizing) shows explicit arithmetic
- [ ] PII/PHI fields explicitly identified + Shield Platform Encryption posture documented
- [ ] Reusability section names ≥3 concrete accelerators (not vague "leverage best practices")
- [ ] Risk register has ≥5 rows with risk + likelihood + impact + mitigation + owner
- [ ] References section cites SFDC Trailhead / official docs / vendor docs (no marketing pages)
- [ ] Cross-section consistency: entities in Section 4 appear in Sections 6 and 7
- [ ] Verbosity within ±20% of FNOL example anchor for similar complexity
- [ ] All ⚠️ ASSUMPTION markers paired with explicit user-validation request
- [ ] Lucidchart instructions in Section 5 (NOT Mermaid)

